243:     void * buf;
244: 
245:     /*
246:      * Invalid streams can refer to fbufs that have not been
247:      * initialized yet. For example the stream could start with a
248:      * picture type onther than I. Or it could have a B picture before
249:      * it gets two reference frames. Or, some slices could be missing.
250:      *
251:      * Consequently, the output depends on the content 2 output
252:      * buffers have when the sequence begins. In release builds, this
253:      * does not matter (garbage in, garbage out), but in test code, we
254:      * always zero all our output buffers to:
255:      * - make our test produce deterministic outputs
256:      * - hint checkergcc that it is fine to read from all our output
257:      *   buffers at any time
